[1.005, "o", "\r\n\u001b[0;36m\u001b[1m━━━ Step 3: /plan — Create a plan from the specification ━━━\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[1.009, "o", "Running: claude -p '/plan ./specification/index.md'\r\n\r\n"]
[319.308, "o", "No problem — the board already bakes in the recommended defaults for all four (single f64, error on divide-by-zero, core arithmetic only, colon commands), so it's ready as-is. If you want any of those changed later, just say so and I'll update the relevant tasks.\r\n\r\nThe board **is** the plan — 9 tasks, all dependencies wired, task 1 (scaffold) ready and the rest correctly blocked behind their prerequisites.\r\n\r\n**Next steps — your call:**\r\n- `/finish` — drives the tasks to `done` autonomously (implement → test → review)\r\n- `/implement` — work them one at a time, starting with the scaffold task\r\n\r\nI won't start implementing until you choose.\r\n"]
