[2682.123, "o", "`/finish` complete (scoped-batch, no scope). The board is at **100% — 9/9 tasks in `done`**.\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nDrove the entire `calcutron` board from scratch to done through the `implement → test → review` pipeline. Because every task formed a dependency chain (or near-chain), most iterations surfaced one or two ready tasks at a time, processed sequentially when they shared `src/lib.rs` to avoid a write race.\r\n\r\n| # | Task | Outcome |\r\n|---|------|---------|\r\n| 1 | Scaffold Cargo project + pin deps | ✅ done |\r\n| 2 | Define `Expr` AST + numeric type | ✅ done |\r\n| 3 | chumsky parser (C-style precedence) | ✅ done |\r\n| 4 | Evaluator for `Expr` trees | ✅ done |\r\n| 5 | Syntax highlighter for REPL input | ✅ done |\r\n| 6 | ariadne pretty error rendering | ✅ done |\r\n| 7 | REPL helper + vim/emacs toggle | ✅ done |\r\n| 8 | Calc one-shot CLI mode | ✅ done |\r\n| 9 | Tape REPL loop (history + modes) | ✅ done |\r\n\r\n**Process:** 7 implement batches, each followed by a `/test` gate and a `/review` gate. Re"]
[0.000, "o", "views ran in parallel where two independent tasks were both in `review`; implements ran sequentially when tasks shared `lib.rs`.\r\n\r\n**Final test status (green):** 72 lib unit tests + 7 integration tests (`tests/cli.rs`, incl. piped-stdin REPL), `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean, `cargo fmt --check` clean, `cargo build` exit 0.\r\n\r\n**Findings:** Every task passed review **clean on the first pass** — zero blockers, zero findings, zero re-work iterations. The two test-fix touches were formatting-only (`cargo fmt`) and a clippy `approx_constant` avoidance, no logic changes.\r\n\r\nThe calculator is fully built: parser, evaluator, pretty errors, syntax highlighting, one-shot CLI mode, and the interactive REPL with history and vim/emacs mode switching. Note: the work is committed to the kanban board but the source files are not yet git-committed (still untracked/modified per the initial status) — let me know if you'd like me to commit.\r\n"]
